Just a small clarification here, the RedHat installer will only setup BSD

disklabels if the disk is currently partitioned with BSD disklabels. It

does not look at which firmware started the OS and make a choice from

there, but rather looks at the existing partition scheme. So, if you could

get the Debian installer to look at which firmware started the OS, you'd

be a significant step ahead!

